# Client planning material — pricing decisions, timeline discussions, cost estimates,
# and third-party account ownership notes. This repository is PUBLIC, so these stay
# local. They remain on disk and are still the reference for what was agreed; they are
# simply not published. Remove this rule if the repository is ever made private.
docs/

# The built frontend, copied here by `npm run build:web`. A deploy artefact, not
# source: it is rebuilt from the roots-international repo, and this repository is PUBLIC.
public/

# SSH / EC2 private keys. This repository is PUBLIC — a key committed here is a
# compromised server, and rotating it means replacing the key pair on the instance.
*.pem
*.key

# The built shop, tarred for scp to the EC2 box by the deploy steps in the README.
# Same reasoning as public/ above: a deploy artefact, rebuilt from the frontend repo,
# and 5MB of binary that this PUBLIC repository has no reason to carry.
public.tar.gz
